WEBVTT

00:00:29.942 --> 00:00:31.987
Evasive maneuvers!

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:34.077
Fire at will!

00:00:37.297 --> 00:00:38.777
We're being boarded!

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.735
Then let's throw them
a welcoming party.

00:00:44.870 --> 00:00:47.307
The device, hand it over!

00:00:47.351 --> 00:00:50.136
I'll destroy this
before I let y-- aah!

00:00:52.095 --> 00:00:54.271
Temba!

00:01:02.235 --> 00:01:04.585
Commanders, the asset
has been obtained.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:06.152
Excellent.

00:01:06.196 --> 00:01:08.720
Destroy this joke
of a Federation ship.

00:01:08.763 --> 00:01:10.852
Leave no survivors.

00:01:14.247 --> 00:01:16.119
All decks!

00:01:16.162 --> 00:01:18.991
I hoped I would never have
to give this order, but...

00:01:19.034 --> 00:01:21.776
- all hands to es--
- Captain, incoming ship.

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:24.301
It's the &lt;i&gt;Wayfarer.&lt;/i&gt;

00:01:30.568 --> 00:01:31.699
- No!
- Ugh!

00:01:31.743 --> 00:01:33.179
Thank the Prophets.

00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:34.833
Send those thanks

00:01:34.876 --> 00:01:37.836
&lt;i&gt;to Captain Bucephalus Dagger.&lt;/i&gt;

00:02:52.432 --> 00:02:54.086
Commander Doodle,
I think it's time

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:56.567
we introduce this warbird
to the biggest kid on the block.

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.699
You heard the Cap.
Target those disruptors.

00:03:03.965 --> 00:03:06.490
Dagger? Get us out of here.

00:03:06.533 --> 00:03:08.361
No! I want his head!

00:03:08.405 --> 00:03:10.842
Don't be greedy, sister.
We've already won.

00:03:10.885 --> 00:03:13.366
They just don't know it yet.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:14.715
Captain, they're retreating.

00:03:14.759 --> 00:03:16.282
Should I set a course to pursue?

00:03:16.326 --> 00:03:17.762
Let 'em run.

00:03:17.805 --> 00:03:19.503
Protecting the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; is
our top priority.

00:03:19.546 --> 00:03:21.331
You're late, Dagger.

00:03:21.374 --> 00:03:23.898
What you do, stop for raktajino?

00:03:23.942 --> 00:03:27.075
What were the Melponar
triplets after this time?

00:03:27.119 --> 00:03:28.990
The Chronogami.

00:03:29.034 --> 00:03:31.079
A top-secret
Starfleet prototype

00:03:31.123 --> 00:03:33.430
which can penetrate
temporal barriers.

00:03:33.473 --> 00:03:36.302
"Chrono" because it involves
taking time,

00:03:36.346 --> 00:03:39.087
and folding it on itself
like the Japanese artform--

00:03:39.131 --> 00:03:41.089
Yeah, origami, right,
yeah, we-we get it.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.917
I thought the Chronogami
was theoretical.

00:03:42.961 --> 00:03:44.702
Well, consider
the theory proved.

00:03:44.745 --> 00:03:46.312
- And now the Romulans have it.

00:03:46.356 --> 00:03:47.313
And I bet my pips

00:03:47.357 --> 00:03:48.445
- they're going...

00:03:48.488 --> 00:03:50.055
Computer, freeze program.

00:03:50.098 --> 00:03:51.752
&lt;i&gt;
Ensign Boimler,&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:51.796 --> 00:03:53.276
&lt;i&gt;please report
to Commander Ransom's office.&lt;/i&gt;

00:03:53.319 --> 00:03:55.278
- On my way.
- I thought you were off duty.

00:03:55.321 --> 00:03:57.845
I am. Ransom just
probably wants me to spot him.

00:03:57.889 --> 00:03:59.891
He just learned
Tellarite deadlifts.

00:03:59.934 --> 00:04:01.980
Whoa, baby!
That opening was awesome, Boims.

00:04:02.023 --> 00:04:04.939
Yeah, but time travel?
Listen, "Captain Dagger."

00:04:04.983 --> 00:04:06.941
Don't tell me we're gonna have
to go back and assassinate

00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:08.421
Kennedy
because that is not happening.

00:04:08.465 --> 00:04:10.205
Okay, don't worry.

00:04:10.249 --> 00:04:13.600
&lt;i&gt;Crisis Point II&lt;/i&gt; is twice
as good as the original.

00:04:13.644 --> 00:04:16.255
&lt;i&gt;Crisis Point?&lt;/i&gt; No! You can't
just piggyback off my movie.

00:04:16.299 --> 00:04:17.952
Technically, it was
my program first.

00:04:17.996 --> 00:04:19.214
So I can do what I want.

00:04:19.258 --> 00:04:21.042
Uh, Computer, arch.

00:04:21.086 --> 00:04:22.479
That doesn't contractually
obligate you

00:04:22.522 --> 00:04:24.524
- to make a bad sequel.
- Is this a sequel?

00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:25.960
I mean, Vindicta got blown up.

00:04:26.004 --> 00:04:27.571
You don't follow the villain.

00:04:27.614 --> 00:04:28.789
We're back with
the &lt;i&gt;Cerritos&lt;/i&gt; bridge crew.

00:04:28.833 --> 00:04:30.400
Trust me, you're gonna love it.

00:04:30.443 --> 00:04:33.011
It's got everything:
action, adventure, romance.

00:04:33.054 --> 00:04:35.535
I'll skip ahead to
the opening credits, uh, okay.

00:04:35.579 --> 00:04:38.190
Freeman just explained
that the Chronogami can be used

00:04:38.233 --> 00:04:40.366
to destroy any point in history.

00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:43.064
What, does it make an alternate
cinematic timeline that runs

00:04:43.108 --> 00:04:44.892
concurrent to our own,
but with, like, different people

00:04:44.936 --> 00:04:46.590
playing younger versions of us?

00:04:46.633 --> 00:04:50.071
Uh, scientifically that
would be a bit of a reach.

00:04:50.115 --> 00:04:51.551
Whatever. If you're
expanding the Vindictaverse,

00:04:51.595 --> 00:04:53.379
I'm just saying
it better not suck.

00:04:53.423 --> 00:04:55.250
Let me know if you want some
hot sauce while you're eating

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.904
those words in the third act.

00:04:56.948 --> 00:04:59.254
I'll be right back.

00:05:03.737 --> 00:05:05.739
Ooh!

00:05:07.001 --> 00:05:08.525
Wait, what's
my character's name again?

00:05:08.568 --> 00:05:10.527
Looks like you're Chief Engineer

00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:12.833
- Sylvo Toussant.
- Ooh, Cajun?

00:05:12.877 --> 00:05:14.966
: &lt;i&gt;
Mon cheri,&lt;/i&gt; I guarantee

00:05:15.009 --> 00:05:16.663
I can do that...

00:05:16.707 --> 00:05:18.578
: Nah, I'm
just gonna play it straight.

00:05:18.622 --> 00:05:20.841
I play Lieutenant Commander
Meena Vesper,

00:05:20.885 --> 00:05:22.495
Whose love of science
and exploration

00:05:22.539 --> 00:05:23.888
is tempered
by her troubled childhood.

00:05:23.931 --> 00:05:26.281
This is such fan fiction.

00:05:26.325 --> 00:05:27.326
All right,
I've got an evaluation

00:05:27.370 --> 00:05:28.414
with Ransom at 1900.

00:05:28.458 --> 00:05:30.329
Boims better not draw this out.

00:05:31.896 --> 00:05:34.028
Ah, the auteur has returned.

00:05:34.072 --> 00:05:35.987
What did, uh,
what did Ransom want?

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:38.468
Uh, just reassigning
duty shifts.

00:05:38.511 --> 00:05:39.512
Oh, the credits are ending.

00:05:39.556 --> 00:05:40.992
Let's get back in character.

00:05:44.909 --> 00:05:46.214
Rutherford, shh!

00:05:54.048 --> 00:05:56.181
The Chronogami Project was
headed up by...

00:05:56.224 --> 00:05:58.357
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
Dr. Helena Gibson.

00:05:58.401 --> 00:06:00.794
Bucephalus.

00:06:00.838 --> 00:06:03.449
Oh, you have got some nerve

00:06:03.493 --> 00:06:05.799
never calling me back
after that weekend on Risa.

00:06:05.843 --> 00:06:07.540
Oh, ho, ho, ho, spicy!

00:06:07.584 --> 00:06:09.629
Oh, so this gorgeous scientist

00:06:09.673 --> 00:06:11.805
is the estranged love interest?
Yeah, sure.

00:06:11.849 --> 00:06:13.851
I'm here for your research,
not your heart.

00:06:13.894 --> 00:06:15.548
Look, the Romulans have
the Chromogami.

00:06:15.592 --> 00:06:17.637
Oh, of-of course.

00:06:24.514 --> 00:06:26.472
Whoa, these
graphics are mind-blowing!

00:06:26.516 --> 00:06:28.256
Rutherford.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:30.302
We've learned there
are space-time worldlines

00:06:30.345 --> 00:06:32.130
that prevent
the beginning of existence

00:06:32.173 --> 00:06:34.132
from merging with the end.

00:06:34.175 --> 00:06:37.091
The Chronogami's gravitons
essentially fold worldlines,

00:06:37.135 --> 00:06:40.138
allowing a user
to travel to the past

00:06:40.181 --> 00:06:42.227
or the future.

00:06:44.664 --> 00:06:47.362
The Romulans could attack
any place and any time,

00:06:47.406 --> 00:06:50.496
allowing them to wipe the
Federation from ever existing.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:52.716
So many lives
just blinked out of existence.

00:06:52.759 --> 00:06:54.457
We could run
a long-range scan...

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:56.197
And to think, you go to bed
probably still thinking

00:06:56.241 --> 00:06:59.200
about some task you have to do
the next day, then poof.

00:06:59.244 --> 00:07:00.767
- You're gone.
- Geez.

00:07:00.811 --> 00:07:02.552
Somebody took
a Winger Bingston acting class.

00:07:02.595 --> 00:07:04.423
You can track the Chronogami
with this.

00:07:04.467 --> 00:07:07.208
It has limited
Chronogamic functionality.

00:07:07.252 --> 00:07:08.558
Ah, yes,
a watch that drives the plot.

00:07:08.601 --> 00:07:10.298
Very convenient
and not at all dumb.

00:07:10.342 --> 00:07:12.170
It detects the chronitons.

00:07:12.213 --> 00:07:13.954
It'll lead you right to them.

00:07:13.998 --> 00:07:16.304
Looks like they're heading
for Tatasciore IX.

00:07:16.348 --> 00:07:18.437
A favorite of black-market
weapons dealers.

00:07:18.481 --> 00:07:20.526
They're probably trying
to buy Wallerian Dutronium

00:07:20.570 --> 00:07:22.528
to power
the Chronogasmic matrix!

00:07:22.572 --> 00:07:24.095
Yeah, Doc,
you really want to avoid

00:07:24.138 --> 00:07:25.400
that many made-up words
in a row.

00:07:25.444 --> 00:07:27.533
All right, uh, this where we set

00:07:27.577 --> 00:07:30.057
a course for Tatasciore IX,
so let's do that.

00:07:30.101 --> 00:07:31.711
Wait, Bucephalus.

00:07:31.755 --> 00:07:33.757
Could we talk... privately?

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.586
Ooh, here comes the romance
in three, two...

00:07:36.629 --> 00:07:38.849
No thanks, I-I-I-I got to go.

00:07:38.892 --> 00:07:40.546
"No thanks"?

00:07:40.590 --> 00:07:42.505
Wait, you can't cut out
the romantic subplot.

00:07:42.548 --> 00:07:44.507
A good movie's got
to have some romance.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:46.465
Dagger's love life
doesn't matter anymore.

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:48.511
Wait, then why'd you design her
so hot?

00:07:48.554 --> 00:07:50.643
I don't know what to do now.

00:07:50.687 --> 00:07:53.080
Uh, yeah. Me, either, lady.
Okay, bye.

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:04.091
Do you feel lost in your way?

00:08:04.135 --> 00:08:05.789
Let Minooki guide you.

00:08:05.832 --> 00:08:07.225
We have to find the Romulans

00:08:07.268 --> 00:08:08.792
or the universe
could cease to exist.

00:08:08.835 --> 00:08:10.707
We're all holograms
in a simulation.

00:08:10.750 --> 00:08:13.579
The koala smiles on us all.

00:08:13.623 --> 00:08:15.320
Ki-ty-ha has the true answers

00:08:15.363 --> 00:08:18.018
for life's
most important questions.

00:08:18.062 --> 00:08:20.020
Okay, feels like
we're just moments away

00:08:20.064 --> 00:08:21.718
from a big set piece, aren't we?

00:08:21.761 --> 00:08:23.415
What are we talking, a heist?
Chase?

00:08:23.458 --> 00:08:25.722
Yo, Earth to Dagger,
I asked if there's gonna be,

00:08:25.765 --> 00:08:27.027
like, a cool chase or something.

00:08:27.071 --> 00:08:28.333
I need answers.

00:08:28.376 --> 00:08:29.856
Then you seek Ki-ty-ha.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.859
Legend says he resides
on the forbidden moon.

00:08:32.903 --> 00:08:34.861
What are you doing?
The holodeck just populated

00:08:34.905 --> 00:08:36.689
that guy into the background
for color.

00:08:36.733 --> 00:08:38.604
I sense Purplehead knows much.

00:08:38.648 --> 00:08:40.998
If one such as he
is drawn to this place,

00:08:41.041 --> 00:08:42.477
- so shall he who is I.
- What in the

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.088
alien of the week bull[bleep]?

00:08:44.131 --> 00:08:45.611
Okay, boys, come on.
We have a movie to do, man.

00:08:45.655 --> 00:08:47.265
We don't have time
to chat up the extras.

00:08:47.308 --> 00:08:48.658
It's an adaptive program.

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:50.660
The-the holodeck's
creating meaning

00:08:50.703 --> 00:08:52.531
- for these guys...
- I've got a lock!

00:08:52.575 --> 00:08:54.664
Aah!

00:08:56.753 --> 00:08:58.537
Gravcycles, mount up.

00:08:58.581 --> 00:09:00.583
Oh, hell yeah!
Now we're talking.

00:09:00.626 --> 00:09:02.454
Dude, come on, we got to grav!

00:09:06.153 --> 00:09:07.807
Come on, we're missing
the sequence!

00:09:07.851 --> 00:09:09.635
No, we need to find Kit-ty-ha.

00:09:09.679 --> 00:09:11.811
Dagger to Vesper, take command
of the Chronogami mission.

00:09:11.855 --> 00:09:13.291
You are acting captain now.

00:09:13.334 --> 00:09:14.988
&lt;i&gt;Ah! Oh, my gosh, thank you!&lt;/i&gt;

00:09:15.032 --> 00:09:17.643
We just spent like an hour
getting the backstory

00:09:17.687 --> 00:09:19.689
of your MacGuffin and now
we're not going after it?

00:09:19.732 --> 00:09:21.647
The path to Ki-ty-ha
is perilous,

00:09:21.691 --> 00:09:24.607
but the reward is
all the truths of the universe.

00:09:24.650 --> 00:09:26.870
This could be the key to it all.
We got to do this.

00:09:26.913 --> 00:09:29.002
This? What is "this"?
These random extras?

00:09:29.046 --> 00:09:30.830
- I am Knicknac.
- Case in point.

00:09:30.874 --> 00:09:32.266
Now what the hell does finding

00:09:32.310 --> 00:09:33.746
some weirdo have
to do with your story?

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:35.748
We-We're gonna go find
the meaning of life.

00:09:35.792 --> 00:09:37.141
Th-This is better
than what I wrote.

00:09:37.184 --> 00:09:38.533
This is important.

00:09:38.577 --> 00:09:39.926
"Important"? What? No.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:41.667
This was supposed
to be a thrill ride.

00:09:41.711 --> 00:09:44.278
Ah, that chase sequence
wasn't gonna be fun anyway.

00:09:44.322 --> 00:09:47.194
This is so [bleep] fun!

00:09:47.238 --> 00:09:49.501
- Aah!

00:10:01.165 --> 00:10:03.646
Remind me to never lend you
my gravcycle.

00:10:05.125 --> 00:10:07.214
Oh, [bleep].

00:10:07.258 --> 00:10:09.521
They're activating
the Chronogami!

00:10:11.915 --> 00:10:14.874
Oh, damn it! They've crossed
the origamic threshfold.

00:10:14.918 --> 00:10:16.528
And if we follow,

00:10:16.571 --> 00:10:18.661
we may never be able
to get back to our own time.

00:10:18.704 --> 00:10:20.750
We have to. For Starfleet!

00:10:21.968 --> 00:10:23.927
For Starfleet!

00:10:36.766 --> 00:10:38.071
Where are we?

00:10:38.115 --> 00:10:39.594
2341.

00:10:39.638 --> 00:10:41.074
We're smack dab in the middle

00:10:41.118 --> 00:10:42.946
of the goddamn algae crisis.

00:10:42.989 --> 00:10:46.210
This is the science center
where Ambassador Koro was able

00:10:46.253 --> 00:10:48.647
to communicate
with the algaeic slime mind.

00:10:48.691 --> 00:10:51.128
Every kid learns about this
in school.

00:10:51.171 --> 00:10:52.738
We have to find the Romulans.

00:10:52.782 --> 00:10:54.479
If they kill Koro,
the algae will wipe out

00:10:54.522 --> 00:10:56.916
- every living creature on the--

00:10:56.960 --> 00:10:59.049
Did you leave and get food?

00:10:59.092 --> 00:11:00.920
Oh, yeah, during the whole
time travel light show.

00:11:00.964 --> 00:11:02.705
That stuff always
gets me seasick.

00:11:02.748 --> 00:11:04.097
I stepped out to grab a bite.
You want some?

00:11:04.141 --> 00:11:05.490
No! I-I feel like

00:11:05.533 --> 00:11:07.100
you're not taking
this seriously.

00:11:07.144 --> 00:11:08.754
Uh, yeah, because I'm not.

00:11:08.798 --> 00:11:10.364
Hey, who's that big squid?

00:11:10.408 --> 00:11:12.845
That's Ambassador Koro!
Never mind.

00:11:12.889 --> 00:11:15.195
All right. Keep down,
stay quiet, and spread out.

00:11:15.239 --> 00:11:16.849
- We are looking for--
- Mmm!

00:11:16.893 --> 00:11:18.068
- What?

00:11:18.111 --> 00:11:19.852
You got to have chips.

00:11:22.463 --> 00:11:24.857
Okay, can we please get back
to the real movie?

00:11:24.901 --> 00:11:26.772
Tendi and Ruthie could be,
like, I dunno,

00:11:26.816 --> 00:11:28.905
in Ancient Egypt
riding crocodiles without us.

00:11:28.948 --> 00:11:31.081
Illustor, how do we get
to Ki-ty-ha?

00:11:31.124 --> 00:11:32.909
Ah, to that I have

00:11:32.952 --> 00:11:34.911
a fascinating answer.

00:11:34.954 --> 00:11:37.217
And the answer is...

00:11:37.261 --> 00:11:39.698
- this answer that's about to be

00:11:39.742 --> 00:11:41.569
- coming now.
- He's stalling.

00:11:41.613 --> 00:11:43.484
The holodeck's just building
this dude a backstory

00:11:43.528 --> 00:11:45.660
on the fly.
We are way off book here.

00:11:45.704 --> 00:11:48.751
Oh, I can show you
my back story.

00:11:51.666 --> 00:11:54.278
- Thou art a map.
- No, absolutely not.

00:11:54.321 --> 00:11:55.714
No, this is stupid,
and too literal.

00:11:55.758 --> 00:11:57.455
Quickly, read my saggy skin.

00:11:57.498 --> 00:11:59.457
Ew! No, this guy can't be
part of the Vindictaverse.

00:11:59.500 --> 00:12:01.241
Oh, shut up!

00:12:01.285 --> 00:12:03.200
I went along with your stupid
movie, which, by the way,

00:12:03.243 --> 00:12:04.679
didn't even have a real ending.

00:12:04.723 --> 00:12:06.681
How dare you! It was epic.

00:12:06.725 --> 00:12:08.596
You should be thanking me
for turning your mess

00:12:08.640 --> 00:12:10.424
into a classy story
that means something.

00:12:10.468 --> 00:12:13.036
It is steeped in significance,
wise one.

00:12:13.079 --> 00:12:14.689
- Thank you, Knacknac.
- Knicknac.

00:12:14.733 --> 00:12:16.996
I'm gonna follow
this old man's skin map,

00:12:17.040 --> 00:12:18.955
and I'm gonna find some answers.

00:12:18.998 --> 00:12:21.131
There are others
who will join this quest

00:12:21.174 --> 00:12:23.133
if you lead us, wise Purplehead.

00:12:23.176 --> 00:12:25.309
Great idea,
let's gather the flock.

00:12:25.352 --> 00:12:28.138
No! This goes against everything
the Vindictaverse stood for.

00:12:28.181 --> 00:12:30.575
I was being nice
agreeing to come in here.

00:12:30.618 --> 00:12:32.142
And now you're ruining
my franchise

00:12:32.185 --> 00:12:33.578
and making me late for my evals.

00:12:33.621 --> 00:12:35.101
&lt;i&gt;Crisis Point&lt;/i&gt; was just a sad

00:12:35.145 --> 00:12:36.799
little tantrum
so you could murder the crew.

00:12:36.842 --> 00:12:39.540
This is an important examination
of the human condition.

00:12:39.584 --> 00:12:41.368
Yeah, i.e., bad movie.

00:12:41.412 --> 00:12:42.935
I officially disown &lt;i&gt;
Crisis Point.&lt;/i&gt;

00:12:42.979 --> 00:12:44.458
Computer, arch.

00:12:44.502 --> 00:12:46.025
You know what,
I'm glad you don't like it,

00:12:46.069 --> 00:12:47.505
because you have awful taste.

00:12:47.548 --> 00:12:48.680
Purplehead speaks the truth.

00:12:48.723 --> 00:12:50.160
Oh, you hated mine so much,

00:12:50.203 --> 00:12:52.162
you had to make a sequel, huh?
Whatever.

00:12:52.205 --> 00:12:53.598
Have fun with Knapsack.

00:12:53.641 --> 00:12:55.687
- Knicknac.
- I will!

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:57.602
Awful taste. Awful taste. Me.

00:12:57.645 --> 00:12:59.343
This guy thinks he's gonna find
spiritual truth

00:12:59.386 --> 00:13:01.301
in the holodeck
and I'm the idiot?

00:13:01.345 --> 00:13:02.868
Uh-huh.

00:13:02.912 --> 00:13:04.827
Uh-huh. You've really turned
a corner, Ensign.

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:07.090
Nothing here but praise
from the department heads.

00:13:07.133 --> 00:13:09.092
Nice work, Mariner. Really.

00:13:09.135 --> 00:13:10.354
- Thanks, Commander.
- Hey, uh,

00:13:10.397 --> 00:13:12.008
how's Boimler doing, by the way?

00:13:12.051 --> 00:13:13.487
Annoying. Why?

00:13:13.531 --> 00:13:15.620
Oh, uh, I figured
he would've told you.

00:13:15.663 --> 00:13:18.057
William, his transporter clone
on the &lt;i&gt;Titan?&lt;/i&gt;

00:13:18.101 --> 00:13:19.711
Died this morning.

00:13:19.754 --> 00:13:22.322
- Wha-- Died? What?
- Freak gas leak.

00:13:22.366 --> 00:13:24.934
Neurocine flooded his quarters.
He was asleep.

00:13:24.977 --> 00:13:27.414
Hell of a way to go.
I gave Mr. Boimler the news

00:13:27.458 --> 00:13:29.025
earlier today.
He's on bereavement leave.

00:13:29.068 --> 00:13:30.287
He didn't say anything?

00:13:30.330 --> 00:13:32.811
No. No, i-it didn't come up.

00:13:32.855 --> 00:13:34.334
I'm sure you want
to be there for him.

00:13:34.378 --> 00:13:35.640
When I've got
a case of the blues,

00:13:35.683 --> 00:13:37.337
I lean on my besties
pretty hard.

00:13:37.381 --> 00:13:39.165
I don't know what I'd do
without Honus the bartender,

00:13:39.209 --> 00:13:40.775
Nurse Westlake
and Matt the whale.

00:13:40.819 --> 00:13:42.473
Friends for life.

00:13:42.516 --> 00:13:44.562
Oh, no.

00:13:48.871 --> 00:13:50.568
Ugh, that time fold
was a big one.

00:13:50.611 --> 00:13:53.745
Earth's 20th century. Late.

00:13:53.788 --> 00:13:55.921
I thought the triplets
were trying to destroy

00:13:55.965 --> 00:13:57.053
the Federation.
It doesn't even exist yet.

00:13:57.096 --> 00:13:58.402
Look!

00:13:58.445 --> 00:13:59.925
An ancestor of Ambassador Koro

00:13:59.969 --> 00:14:01.753
is inside that aquarium.

00:14:01.796 --> 00:14:04.190
They're going to take out
his whole family line.

00:14:04.234 --> 00:14:06.932
Oy! Drop the shiny gizmo, mate.

00:14:06.976 --> 00:14:09.456
- Stepped in the wrong place!
- It's our turf, mate.

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.980
Look, we don't want any...

00:14:12.590 --> 00:14:14.200
...witnesses.

00:14:14.244 --> 00:14:16.289
- Oy! Let's get out of here.

00:14:16.333 --> 00:14:18.248
- I think we have

00:14:18.291 --> 00:14:20.859
to kidnap that octopus
and take it to a safe house.

00:14:20.903 --> 00:14:22.556
- Then we--
- Give me that jacket.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.384
- What are you doing?
- I'm robbing these street punks

00:14:24.428 --> 00:14:26.560
so we can all dress up
in these old-timey outfits.

00:14:26.604 --> 00:14:27.692
Yeah, we don't have time
for that.

00:14:27.735 --> 00:14:29.041
But that's, like, the fun part

00:14:29.085 --> 00:14:30.303
of the whole time travel thing.

00:14:30.347 --> 00:14:32.044
No! Stop messing around.

00:14:32.088 --> 00:14:34.525
I'm at least getting the pants.

00:14:36.222 --> 00:14:37.832
Will you please hurry up?

00:14:37.876 --> 00:14:39.399
They don't fit.

00:14:39.443 --> 00:14:41.488
We need to find bigger punks.

00:14:47.059 --> 00:14:48.582
Space freighter?

00:14:48.626 --> 00:14:50.671
Uh, hello? Boimler--

00:14:50.715 --> 00:14:52.282
uh, Captain Dagger?

00:14:52.325 --> 00:14:54.197
Intruder!
Capture the nonbeliever.

00:14:56.721 --> 00:14:58.853
Don't touch me! Your characters
don't even have names.

00:14:58.897 --> 00:15:00.681
You know nothing of our ways.

00:15:00.725 --> 00:15:02.335
Acolyte 2,

00:15:02.379 --> 00:15:03.946
throw her into the brig.

00:15:07.906 --> 00:15:10.604
I'm friends with
the lead character, you idiots.

00:15:10.648 --> 00:15:12.041
Hey.

00:15:14.173 --> 00:15:15.479
What are you doing in here?

00:15:15.522 --> 00:15:17.394
The tattoo map was a total bust.

00:15:17.437 --> 00:15:18.961
I couldn't find Ki-ty-ha.

00:15:19.004 --> 00:15:21.441
Then my followers got pissed
and mutinied.

00:15:21.485 --> 00:15:24.096
I can't make a good movie.
I can hardly make a bad one.

00:15:24.140 --> 00:15:26.011
It fell apart
right after you left.

00:15:28.840 --> 00:15:31.843
Yeah, so, Ransom told me
about William.

00:15:31.886 --> 00:15:33.976
I'm so sorry.
You must feel terrible.

00:15:34.019 --> 00:15:35.281
Why didn't you say something?

00:15:35.325 --> 00:15:36.848
Ah, I haven't
really processed it.

00:15:36.891 --> 00:15:38.937
I mean,
he was an exact copy of me.

00:15:38.981 --> 00:15:40.939
Had his own quarters
on a cooler ship,

00:15:40.983 --> 00:15:43.507
but he died for no reason.

00:15:43.550 --> 00:15:46.292
I guess I was trying to make all
of this matter because then...

00:15:46.336 --> 00:15:48.425
I would matter.

00:15:48.468 --> 00:15:50.079
But trying to make
this dumb movie important

00:15:50.122 --> 00:15:51.732
just proved that I'm not.

00:15:51.776 --> 00:15:53.343
It's just a holodeck program.

00:15:53.386 --> 00:15:55.040
I know, I was stupid.

00:15:55.084 --> 00:15:57.303
Let's just get out of here.
Computer, arch.

00:15:57.347 --> 00:15:59.131
Cancel arch.

00:15:59.175 --> 00:16:01.046
- Mariner...
- I found deeper meaning

00:16:01.090 --> 00:16:03.309
in &lt;i&gt;Rise of Vindicta,&lt;/i&gt;
and it was totally unscripted.

00:16:03.353 --> 00:16:04.702
If I did it, you can, too.

00:16:04.745 --> 00:16:06.138
But it's a bad story.

00:16:06.182 --> 00:16:08.184
Yeah, it's an uneven slog
that totally ignores

00:16:08.227 --> 00:16:09.707
the successes of the original.

00:16:09.750 --> 00:16:11.926
But it's also a Starfleet movie,

00:16:11.970 --> 00:16:13.493
which means it's worth doing.

00:16:13.537 --> 00:16:15.626
Yeah, it is a Starfleet movie.

00:16:15.669 --> 00:16:17.323
We are Starfleet.

00:16:17.367 --> 00:16:19.064
yeah, we're Starfleet.

00:16:19.108 --> 00:16:21.066
Yes! Okay, uh, okay, first

00:16:21.110 --> 00:16:23.460
we have to figure
a way out of this brig.

00:16:25.636 --> 00:16:27.029
Knicknac!

00:16:27.072 --> 00:16:29.074
I never stopped believing
in you, Purplehead.

00:16:29.118 --> 00:16:32.077
I love you.
I'm in love with you.

00:16:32.121 --> 00:16:33.948
I'm in love with you too, buddy.
Let's go.

00:16:33.992 --> 00:16:36.081
Okay, hey, there's your romance.

00:16:37.865 --> 00:16:40.477
With the power of Ki-ty-ha,
all of creation

00:16:40.520 --> 00:16:42.435
will be in my control.

00:16:42.479 --> 00:16:44.220
Oh, shut up.
You're just a fleshy map.

00:16:44.263 --> 00:16:45.743
Acolytes!

00:16:45.786 --> 00:16:48.485
Throw these nonbelievers
out the holy airlock.

00:16:48.528 --> 00:16:50.704
You have no power here!

00:16:50.748 --> 00:16:52.489
We're all searching
for greater meaning,

00:16:52.532 --> 00:16:54.273
and it's not you.

00:16:54.317 --> 00:16:56.493
Here it comes, the big heroic
speech where you turn him

00:16:56.536 --> 00:16:58.712
- around from being--

00:16:58.756 --> 00:17:00.149
Or, yeah, we can do
the Kirk thing.

00:17:00.192 --> 00:17:01.672
That's cool, too.

00:17:04.109 --> 00:17:06.024
Knicknac!

00:17:06.068 --> 00:17:08.113
Damn, okay,
third act Knicknac reveal.

00:17:08.157 --> 00:17:09.506
Come here!

00:17:16.600 --> 00:17:19.124
- Feel better?
- Uh, yeah, a little.

00:17:19.168 --> 00:17:21.953
But... [gasps] Look at this.

00:17:21.996 --> 00:17:24.260
If I pull these two folds
of skin together...

00:17:25.435 --> 00:17:27.524
The map to Ki-ty-ha.

00:17:36.054 --> 00:17:38.230
Careful! That bomb has
a hair trigger.

00:17:38.274 --> 00:17:40.406
Wait, how does this play
into the octopus stuff?

00:17:40.450 --> 00:17:42.147
I think the Romulans
gave up on that.

00:17:42.191 --> 00:17:43.801
Now they're just trying
to blow up the founders

00:17:43.844 --> 00:17:45.324
before they found
the Federation.

00:17:45.368 --> 00:17:47.370
I hope you know what
you're doing, Toussant.

00:17:47.413 --> 00:17:50.024
&lt;i&gt;♪ Chu-chu, chu-chu-choo...♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:17:50.068 --> 00:17:52.375
Rutherford, will you stop
around?!

00:17:52.418 --> 00:17:54.072
If that thing explodes,
then there's no Federation.

00:17:54.116 --> 00:17:57.336
Sorry, I've got that Chu Chu
song stuck in my head.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:58.555
It's such an earworm.

00:17:58.598 --> 00:18:00.513
&lt;i&gt;♪ Chu-chu, chu-choo...♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:00.557 --> 00:18:02.124
&lt;i&gt;♪ I almost got it♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:02.167 --> 00:18:03.299
- Die.

00:18:03.342 --> 00:18:05.692
No...

00:18:05.736 --> 00:18:07.433
&lt;i&gt;♪ Got it, chu-chu...♪&lt;/i&gt;

00:18:09.087 --> 00:18:10.915
No!

00:18:10.958 --> 00:18:12.656
No, no, no, no, no.
Stay with me, Dr. T.

00:18:12.699 --> 00:18:14.048
You're gonna be okay.

00:18:14.092 --> 00:18:18.531
Don't bull

00:18:21.665 --> 00:18:23.057
Ooh.

00:18:23.101 --> 00:18:25.451
Smells like fried Romulan
in here, huh, guys?

00:18:25.495 --> 00:18:27.540
Whoo, someone crack a window.

00:18:27.584 --> 00:18:28.933
Damn it, Rutherford!

00:18:28.976 --> 00:18:31.022
Why aren't you taking this
seriously?

00:18:31.065 --> 00:18:33.067
'Cause we're having fun.
What's the big deal?

00:18:33.111 --> 00:18:35.200
This isn't fun for me.
Would you laugh this much

00:18:35.244 --> 00:18:36.941
if I was really the captain
in real life?

00:18:36.984 --> 00:18:38.377
Sorry, if you were what?

00:18:38.421 --> 00:18:39.770
Nobody would believe in me
as a captain.

00:18:39.813 --> 00:18:41.511
You don't even care about
this story at all.

00:18:41.554 --> 00:18:43.991
- You want to be a captain?
- Yes!

00:18:44.035 --> 00:18:46.211
Oh, wow, I've never said that
out loud before.

00:18:46.255 --> 00:18:48.344
Yes. Yes, I do.

00:18:48.387 --> 00:18:50.259
Tendi, you'd be a great captain.

00:18:50.302 --> 00:18:51.825
You don't need a movie
to prove that.

00:18:51.869 --> 00:18:53.740
- Really?
- Are you kidding?

00:18:53.784 --> 00:18:55.699
I'd want you
as my captain anytime.

00:18:55.742 --> 00:18:58.267
I can't even tell you
what that means to me.

00:18:58.310 --> 00:19:00.486
Captain Vesper,
your crew is ready.

00:19:00.530 --> 00:19:02.009
What are your orders?

00:19:02.053 --> 00:19:05.056
It's time to take a page
from the Melponar's book.

00:19:20.158 --> 00:19:23.335
Evasive maneuvers!
Fire at will.

00:19:27.513 --> 00:19:28.819
We're being boarded.

00:19:28.862 --> 00:19:31.909
Let's throw them
a welcoming party.

00:19:33.911 --> 00:19:35.478
- Just take it. Don't hurt me.

00:19:35.521 --> 00:19:38.307
Ha. Federation coward.

00:19:38.350 --> 00:19:39.612
Temba.

00:19:41.832 --> 00:19:43.268
&lt;i&gt;
Commanders,&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:43.312 --> 00:19:45.966
- the asset has been attained.
- Excellent.

00:19:46.010 --> 00:19:48.882
Destroy this joke
of a Federation ship.

00:19:48.926 --> 00:19:50.971
&lt;i&gt;TENDI [over comm]:
Joke's on you.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:51.015 --> 00:19:53.017
Identify yourself.
Who is this?

00:19:53.060 --> 00:19:54.627
This is acting Captain
Meena Vesper.

00:19:54.671 --> 00:19:56.020
&lt;i&gt;You're too late.&lt;/i&gt;

00:19:56.063 --> 00:19:57.761
With the Chronogami,
we will destroy

00:19:57.804 --> 00:19:59.502
everything you hold dear.

00:19:59.545 --> 00:20:01.286
That would be true
if you had the Chronogami,

00:20:01.330 --> 00:20:02.853
and not your own bomb.

00:20:04.420 --> 00:20:07.205
- No!

00:20:09.381 --> 00:20:11.253
Tendi, you did it!

00:20:11.296 --> 00:20:13.603
Ha-ha! Way to go, Captain.

00:20:34.188 --> 00:20:36.016
There.

00:20:39.498 --> 00:20:41.152
Whoa!

00:20:50.292 --> 00:20:52.294
I am Ki-ty-ha.

00:20:52.337 --> 00:20:54.339
You have journeyed far.

00:20:54.383 --> 00:20:56.733
What truth do you seek?

00:20:57.734 --> 00:20:59.562
A man named William Boimler died.

00:20:59.605 --> 00:21:02.826
It was meaningless.
What is life for?

00:21:02.869 --> 00:21:06.786
The purpose of life...

00:21:06.830 --> 00:21:10.312
is a life of purpose.

00:21:11.400 --> 00:21:14.098
Okay. But what about
what I was asking?

00:21:14.141 --> 00:21:18.537
Love without trust is
a river without water.

00:21:18.581 --> 00:21:20.931
Yeah, these are just
inspirational quotes.

00:21:20.974 --> 00:21:23.194
I-I Wanted the meaning
of life.

00:21:23.237 --> 00:21:25.327
Life is like a cup of tea.

00:21:25.370 --> 00:21:26.763
It's all in how you steep

00:21:26.806 --> 00:21:28.199
- the water.
- Are you [bleep] kidding me?

00:21:28.242 --> 00:21:29.896
You're supposed to be
the Almighty.

00:21:29.940 --> 00:21:32.464
Oh, there's always a catch
with these "god" stories.

00:21:32.508 --> 00:21:34.814
The holodeck just made
a cheesy quote generator.

00:21:34.858 --> 00:21:37.251
But we came all this way.
I want answers.

00:21:37.295 --> 00:21:39.602
Laughter and
a good night's sleep will...

00:21:39.645 --> 00:21:41.604
Shut up.

00:21:43.257 --> 00:21:45.390
Not every holodeck movie
is gonna work as therapy.

00:21:45.434 --> 00:21:46.913
Why don't we head over
to Migleemo's office

00:21:46.957 --> 00:21:49.133
and he'll tell us some recipes.

00:21:50.177 --> 00:21:52.136
The real answers
must be in there.

00:21:52.179 --> 00:21:53.964
KI-TY-HA:
Ow. Ow! Stop, that hurts.

00:21:54.007 --> 00:21:55.400
Oh, Boimler, come on.

00:21:55.444 --> 00:21:57.010
Don't-- You don't want to
crawl in there, man.

00:21:57.054 --> 00:21:59.273
That thing's putting off
a lot of heat.

00:22:10.546 --> 00:22:11.938
Kitty Hawk?

00:22:11.982 --> 00:22:14.158
Kitty Hawk?!

00:22:14.201 --> 00:22:17.204
That reveal doesn't
make any sense. Ugh!

00:22:17.248 --> 00:22:19.381
My movie is trash.

00:22:19.424 --> 00:22:21.034
It doesn't have
a deeper meaning,

00:22:21.078 --> 00:22:23.167
and neither does life.

00:22:23.210 --> 00:22:25.561
I should have stayed
a raisin farmer.

00:22:25.604 --> 00:22:27.693
I could have
married Lianne.

00:22:38.878 --> 00:22:42.665
Where am I? Mariner?

00:22:47.234 --> 00:22:49.759
Steady. Steady, Atlas.

00:22:52.588 --> 00:22:54.546
Uh, uh, Captain Kirk?

00:22:54.590 --> 00:22:56.287
Oh, my, no.

00:22:56.330 --> 00:22:57.680
It's Captain Sulu.

00:22:57.723 --> 00:23:00.030
Oh, my gosh, Captain Sulu.
Even better.

00:23:00.073 --> 00:23:02.206
Uh, sorry about that.
The-the mailbox said...

00:23:02.249 --> 00:23:04.295
I took this place
off Kirk's hands.

00:23:04.338 --> 00:23:07.864
He had to go and time travel,
or who knows what.

00:23:07.907 --> 00:23:10.432
The man could never relax.

00:23:10.475 --> 00:23:12.346
What-what is this place?

00:23:12.390 --> 00:23:14.131
Pretty nice spread, right?

00:23:14.174 --> 00:23:16.220
There's even a hot tub
in the back.

00:23:16.263 --> 00:23:19.179
Is this heaven? The afterlife?
The Nexus?

00:23:19.223 --> 00:23:22.705
It's Idaho. Would you like
to feed the horsey?

00:23:22.748 --> 00:23:25.229
Uh, sure.

00:23:25.272 --> 00:23:28.188
I-I didn't program
any of this.

00:23:28.232 --> 00:23:30.756
I was in the holodeck
trying to find meaning

00:23:30.800 --> 00:23:32.062
in the randomness of death,

00:23:32.105 --> 00:23:34.238
but I just made a fool
of myself.

00:23:34.281 --> 00:23:37.284
Brad, I've lost many friends.

00:23:37.328 --> 00:23:41.245
Some heroically,
some tragically.

00:23:41.288 --> 00:23:43.943
The randomness of death
is merely a reflection

00:23:43.987 --> 00:23:47.947
of the unexpected joys
we find in life.

00:23:47.991 --> 00:23:51.124
So if I spend my life worrying
about a meaningless death,

00:23:51.168 --> 00:23:53.083
I'll never find joy?

00:23:53.126 --> 00:23:54.998
I literally just said that.

00:23:55.041 --> 00:23:57.304
Sorry. Thanks, Captain Sulu.

00:23:57.348 --> 00:23:58.741
I think I can live with that.

00:23:58.784 --> 00:24:00.873
Happy to help a fellow
Starfleet officer

00:24:00.917 --> 00:24:02.222
looking for answers.

00:24:02.266 --> 00:24:03.441
Oh, great. Awesome.

00:24:03.485 --> 00:24:04.790
So, can I ask you
what it was like

00:24:04.834 --> 00:24:06.226
working with Spock and Uhura?

00:24:06.270 --> 00:24:07.314
Was it weird using
the crystal buttons

00:24:07.358 --> 00:24:08.838
on the &lt;i&gt;Enterprise?&lt;/i&gt;

00:24:08.881 --> 00:24:10.361
Ooh, did you practice daily
with the sword?

00:24:10.404 --> 00:24:11.971
I'm, uh, kind of a sword guy
myself, so...

00:24:12.015 --> 00:24:13.973
The horsey's going
to bite you now.

00:24:19.152 --> 00:24:22.025
Sulu? How'd I get off
the ranch?

00:24:22.068 --> 00:24:23.069
Yeah, you passed out
screaming something

00:24:23.113 --> 00:24:24.723
about the Wright Brothers.

00:24:24.767 --> 00:24:26.682
Kid, you gotta take
water breaks in there.

00:24:26.725 --> 00:24:29.554
Holodeck might be fake,
but dehydration is real.

00:24:29.598 --> 00:24:31.338
So I was dreaming?

00:24:31.382 --> 00:24:33.166
More like clinically dead.

00:24:33.210 --> 00:24:35.473
Sorry you didn't find out
the meaning of life today.

00:24:35.517 --> 00:24:36.866
You know what,
I think maybe

00:24:36.909 --> 00:24:38.041
I shouldn't have been
looking for it.

00:24:38.084 --> 00:24:39.564
Sorry my movie was a letdown.

00:24:39.608 --> 00:24:42.045
Are you kidding?
It was amazing.

00:24:42.088 --> 00:24:43.568
- Really?
- I don't know

00:24:43.612 --> 00:24:45.004
what you guys got into,

00:24:45.048 --> 00:24:47.224
but our story was sick.
Tendi rocked it.

00:24:47.267 --> 00:24:48.530
Yeah. Ours was great, too.

00:24:48.573 --> 00:24:50.053
Dagger here fought off
a mutiny

00:24:50.096 --> 00:24:51.794
and then beat the
out of a god.

00:24:51.837 --> 00:24:53.186
-  What?
- I want to do that!

00:24:53.230 --> 00:24:54.623
Would you get the hell
out of here?!

00:24:54.666 --> 00:24:56.407
Stevens leaned against
the warp core.

00:24:56.450 --> 00:24:57.800
I need this bed cleared now.

00:24:59.105 --> 00:25:01.412
Oh, not twice in one day!

00:25:01.455 --> 00:25:03.327
Ooh, that was so much fun.

00:25:03.370 --> 00:25:05.068
That hovercycle chase
was intense.

00:25:05.111 --> 00:25:07.026
Yeah. I'm still thinking
about those graphics.

00:25:07.070 --> 00:25:08.637
Ooh, did you guys run into
the punks?

00:25:08.680 --> 00:25:10.769
- Yeah. Oh, they were so punky.
- Oh, man. So good.

00:25:10.813 --> 00:25:12.249
You know what, Boims?
Maybe this was

00:25:12.292 --> 00:25:13.467
a good sequel to &lt;i&gt;Crisis Point.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:13.511 --> 00:25:15.165
Aw, thanks, Mariner.

00:25:15.208 --> 00:25:17.210
I'm glad you didn't end it
on some dark cliffhanger.

00:25:17.254 --> 00:25:18.734
- I like happy endings.
- Ugh.

00:25:18.777 --> 00:25:19.952
&lt;i&gt;
Cliffhangers are the worst.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:19.996 --> 00:25:22.215
&lt;i&gt;I hate when people do that.&lt;/i&gt;

00:25:37.883 --> 00:25:39.624
It-it worked.

00:25:39.668 --> 00:25:41.060
Welcome, William.

00:25:41.104 --> 00:25:43.497
Starfleet now considers you
a dead man.

00:25:43.541 --> 00:25:45.630
Just how we like it.

00:25:50.896 --> 00:25:53.551
Isn't Section 31 supposed to be,
like, a big secret?

00:25:53.595 --> 00:25:55.292
I mean, why would we wear
special combadges

00:25:55.335 --> 00:25:57.424
- that advertise who we are?
- You could still be dead.

00:25:58.991 --> 00:26:00.863
No, no, no, you know--
You know what, I like the badge.

00:26:00.906 --> 00:26:03.169
I like the badge.

00:27:04.100 --> 00:27:08.100
Chirp.
